# Orbit-first documentation voice

Learner-facing Orbit docs (`docs/src/content/docs/**`, gallery captions, features pages) teach **Orbit on its own terms**. Readers are assumed to know **no other admin framework**.

## Required

- Explain every concept from first principles (what it is, why it exists, how to use it in Orbit).
- Use Orbit class/method names, Orbit examples, and Orbit screenshots only.
- Prefer concrete walkthroughs: problem → API → code snippet → light/dark shot when available.
- Cross-link other Orbit docs pages instead of external admin UIs.

## Forbidden in learner docs

- “Mirrors Filament…”, “Filament 5 parity”, “Filament-style”, “Filament-familiar”, “same as Filament”, “Filament’s X”
- Mapping tables that list Filament APIs next to Orbit as the primary explanation
- Assuming the reader already knows Filament (or Laravel admin) vocabulary
- Telling readers to “see Filament docs” for behavior Orbit should document

## Allowed exceptions

- **Maintainer-only** files such as `docs/parity.md` may mention Filament for internal tracking.
- **Historical** release-note bullets that record past work may keep factual changelog wording; do not use them as teaching copy.
- The home page may include a brief optional “inspiration” note that does **not** require Filament knowledge to continue learning.

## When editing or polishing a feature

Rewrite any Filament-referential prose you touch. Expand explanations so a new Orbit learner can succeed without opening another product’s docs.
